    <PostBuildEvent>
      <Command>REM SFML/OpenCV/tesseract are all linked dynamically, and the Windows loader
REM resolves an exe's implicit imports before main() ever runs - so a PATH
REM fix inside the program is too late. Copying the DLLs next to the exe
REM works unconditionally, since the exe's own folder is always the first
REM place the loader looks, no PATH or working-directory setup required.
